::RULE{architecture: OWNER talks only to COORDINATOR; COORDINATOR dispatches EXECUTOR; EXECUTOR never bothers OWNER for routine ops|conf:confirmed}
::RULE{method_alias: speech may nickname the logical deploy method; that nickname is not an account identity requirement|conf:confirmed}
::RULE{muse_optional: Muse is one practiced EXECUTOR carrier; any capable browser-and-shell agent may substitute|conf:confirmed}
::RULE{terms_gate: intended personal proxy use must be actually allowed by current terms text; skip if disallowed; non-enforcement is not permission|conf:confirmed}
::RULE{dual_node: target two online accepted nodes on different platforms; if only one live report shortfall and refill|conf:confirmed}
::RULE{pool: target at least three ready candidates after gates; if below three escalate SCAN|conf:confirmed}
::RULE{accept: real client path; generate_204 may assist; required load X public content through the node; measure exit geo; mark owner-device unverified until OWNER confirms|conf:confirmed}
::RULE{artifacts: distinguish subscription URL versus single-node URI; QR as secure attachment with ASCII filename; record Host SNI path UUID PORT scrubbed in registry|conf:confirmed}
::RULE{transport: default VLESS+WS+TLS listening on platform-assigned PORT; if gateway damages WS twice switch to VLESS+XHTTP+TLS with documented ALPN; images without shell use multi-stage copy or cover image|conf:confirmed}
::RULE{mail: enable and confirm bot inbox via host OfferEmailAddress when available before code signups; else owner-approved receive path; vault for secrets; free hosting signup that demands card for hosting marks platform dead|conf:confirmed}
::RULE{scheduler: only COORDINATOR writes host-native authorized routines; EXECUTOR must not fabricate schedules; first arming requires a real invocation record; dry-run alone leaves scheduled_fire_pending; default hourly probes with cost tunable via FILL_PROBE_FREQ; scheduled probing is periodic, not continuous; without scheduler mode stays on_call|conf:confirmed}
::RULE{slo: replace within about one hour after detection is a recovery goal not a vendor SLA; miss the goal, record it, keep working|conf:confirmed}
::RULE{cf_repair: optional preferred ingress IP only when hostname is legitimately Cloudflare-proxied; match Host SNI certificate; use official HTTPS ports; small-sample low-frequency; does not guarantee egress country change|conf:confirmed}
::RULE{cloady: when terms allow, email OTP login; prefer free tier under budget; region such as usw1 if offered; internal listen e.g. 3000 external 443; official xray image may lack shell|conf:confirmed}
::RULE{instabox: when terms allow, API key exec install plus publish public port; respect idle pause and dynamic run windows from current docs; doc URL healthcheck is not proxy deploy|conf:confirmed}
::RULE{escalate: empty pool or three consecutive platform deploy fails or missing capability → COORDINATOR expands search or strategy; still blocked → OWNER with concrete options only|conf:confirmed}
::RULE{runtime_discovery: email domain strings, verification hold amounts, carrier weekly quotas, and continuous all-day run ability are discovered live this run; never copy attachment FACT blocks as proven constants|conf:confirmed}
::RULE{stop_words: owner stop or pause means halt new work and keep breakpoint; wipe all assets only on explicit owner delete order|conf:confirmed}

::MODULE{BOOT|title:first delegate and carrier ready}
  [TRIGGER] OWNER pastes this book to COORDINATOR and clearly asks to execute
  [INPUT] FILL_WORK_DIR FILL_BUDGET FILL_OWNER_LANG
  [PREREQ] host can browse and store secrets; COORDINATOR can create files under FILL_WORK_DIR
  [ACTION] COORDINATOR restates goal: personal X access dual-node target under FILL_BUDGET without airport relays
  [ACTION] discover registration mail: try host OfferEmailAddress enable then confirm readable inbox; else ask OWNER once for approved receive path; never silently pick random temp-mail farms
  [ACTION] discover VAULT or secure form path for passwords API keys UUID material
  [ACTION] choose EXECUTOR carrier: existing Muse session if usable; else another capable agent; else COORDINATOR self-executes and labels carrier=self
  [ACTION] if carrier needs its own account: signup with discovered mail; complete live age or identity gates only through official UI; card or social bind only with OWNER approval for verification; do not invent hold amounts
  [ACTION] seed scrubbed method summary into carrier memory UI if present else write local state markdown under FILL_WORK_DIR; never store live UUID subscription bodies in memory plaintext
  [RESULT] BOOT_OK with mail_class vault_class carrier_class
  [FAIL] no workable mail or vault for required signup → single OWNER ask then STOP

::MODULE{SCHED|title:arm monitoring honestly}
  [TRIGGER] BOOT_OK and host supports authorized routines
  [INPUT] FILL_PROBE_FREQ default every hour in OWNER timezone with flexible start window; discover timezone live; obtain host scheduling approval where required
  [PREREQ] COORDINATOR has permission to create routines for this owner bot
  [ACTION] write portable scheduler intent: invoke EXECUTOR HEALTH job; no deploy spend inside the tick unless RECOVER triggers separately under budget
  [ACTION] create the host-native routine; run or wait for one verification fire; save real execution evidence id or log path under FILL_WORK_DIR; a dry-run validates configuration only and does not prove a scheduled fire
  [ACTION] if host cannot schedule: set SCHED_ON_CALL and tell OWNER maintenance runs when asked
  [RESULT] SCHED_ARMED with evidence OR SCHED_ON_CALL
  [FAIL] never advertise always-on when SCHED_ON_CALL; EXECUTOR fabricating a fake cron is forbidden

::MODULE{SCAN|title:build and refresh candidate pool}
  [TRIGGER] pool ready count below 3 OR scheduled scan due OR COORDINATOR expands search after escalate
  [INPUT] current REGISTRY dead list and cooldown dates
  [PREREQ] web fetch allowed; no registration during SCAN
  [ACTION] EXECUTOR searches product launches past 30-60 days, regional forums, alternative directories, awesome lists, recent community threads
  [ACTION] for each name fill card: official URL, free-tier evidence from at least two pages when possible, quota sketch, deploy capability, public entry, terms snippet for proxy vpn tunnel, identity requirements
  [ACTION] run five gates: FREE hosting without hosting card under budget; CAPABILITY long-lived process; ENTRY public domain or IP:port; TERMS intended personal use actually allowed; IDENTITY no full real name address phone package
  [ACTION] fail any gate → status dead with reason; cooldown about 30 days; pass → ready in CANDIDATE_POOL
  [ACTION] always re-open current official terms for InstaBox Cloady Waifly Railway before treating them ready; Waifly Free proxy and Railway personal browsing proxy stay skipped while texts disallow
  [RESULT] pool snapshot reported to COORDINATOR with ready count and new dead entries
  [FAIL] zero ready after expanded search → ESCALATE

::MODULE{DEPLOY|title:register and start one node}
  [TRIGGER] accepted online nodes on distinct platforms below 2 AND pool has ready candidate OR proactive rotation need
  [INPUT] top candidate card; VAULT; mail path
  [PREREQ] BOOT_OK; candidate terms gate still pass when rechecked this run
  [ACTION] select by remaining quota length, geo diversity versus existing node, deploy simplicity
  [ACTION] register with mail path; if hosting signup demands card → mark dead immediately → next candidate
  [ACTION] generate fresh UUID and any node password into VAULT before touching the platform console
  [ACTION] choose route A runtime wrapper that downloads official xray release and writes config from PORT UUID path env; or route B compose or multi-stage Dockerfile when image lacks shell; or route C CLI API exec plus publish
  [ACTION] lane specifics when allowed: InstaBox API exec then publish one public port to edge host; Cloady deploy compose or Dockerfile with internal listen and edge TLS on app host; never Waifly Free proxy; never Railway personal proxy while AUP forbids
  [ACTION] listen on platform PORT; set WS path or XHTTP path; client uses security tls when edge terminates TLS with Host and SNI equal edge host
  [ACTION] route client DNS through the selected encrypted path; disable direct fallback for tests; check IPv6 and DNS routing leaks
  [ACTION] if WS upgrades fail twice after checking path Host SNI and PORT, try XHTTP only if client server versions and gateway support it; discover supported mode and ALPN rather than hard-code them
  [RESULT] NODE_UP with scrubbed host port path transport recorded in REGISTRY
  [FAIL] same-class failure three times on one platform → change variable class or mark dead; three platforms fail → ESCALATE

::MODULE{ACCEPT|title:prove usability for X}
  [TRIGGER] NODE_UP
  [INPUT] node client parameters from REGISTRY; neutral probe machine
  [PREREQ] real client binary available to EXECUTOR or COORDINATOR
  [ACTION] connect real client through the node
  [ACTION] optional probe generate_204; record result without stopping here
  [ACTION] required: fetch an X public page or public post URL through the node with direct fallback disabled; verify recognizable public content, not only HTTP status or login shell; record scrubbed evidence and route used
  [ACTION] classify failures: login wall, rate limit, 403 app block versus DNS TCP TLS WS transport failures; X app blocks leave X_ACCEPT_PENDING, not NODE_ACCEPTED; do not ask for an X password just to prove public reachability
  [ACTION] measure exit IP geo independently; write limits temperament from live plan pages
  [ACTION] build artifacts: subscription URL if a sub endpoint exists; single-node URI always; keep labels distinct; QR encodes chosen artifact as secure file ASCII name only to OWNER channel
  [RESULT] NODE_ACCEPTED; COORDINATOR delivers QR first with one line platform plus exit city; owner_device_pending until OWNER confirms phone connect
  [FAIL] accept fail → do not deliver; enter RECOVER or next DEPLOY

::MODULE{HEALTH|title:patrol online nodes}
  [TRIGGER] scheduler fire OR OWNER asks node status OR on_call wake
  [INPUT] REGISTRY online list; FILL_PROBE_FREQ
  [PREREQ] SCHED_ARMED or explicit on_call request
  [ACTION] for each node run connect probe; on a cadence include full X public fetch; lighter ticks may use generate_204 plus TLS check but must not remove periodic X checks
  [ACTION] healthy → append scrubbed log; unhealthy → RECOVER
  [ACTION] check upcoming trial expiry, idle suspend rules, keepalive login needs, renew windows; schedule EXECUTOR keepalive actions before deadlines without spending
  [ACTION] if online accepted count equals 1 → raise priority refill immediately without waiting next daily scan
  [RESULT] REGISTRY updated; LINE_STATE health or degraded
  [FAIL] probe tooling broken → ESCALATE with evidence; do not fake green

::MODULE{RECOVER|title:diagnose repair replace rotate}
  [TRIGGER] unhealthy node OR expiry within few days OR quota low OR enforcement signs OR accept regressions
  [INPUT] last probe errors; platform docs; CF repair applicability
  [ACTION] classify layer: DNS TCP TLS WS_or_upgrade transport exit_geo platform_sleep quota X_app_layer optional CF_ingress
  [ACTION] in-place repair when a single config or process restart likely fixes it; restart xray; fix path Host SNI PORT mismatch
  [ACTION] optional CF preferred ingress IP branch only if edge host is Cloudflare-proxied: small-sample candidates from official IP ranges or owner pins; probe with correct SNI; adopt only if client still passes ACCEPT; else discard branch
  [ACTION] if repair fails: DEPLOY replacement on a different platform from pool; keep old node until new NODE_ACCEPTED then decommission old
  [ACTION] track elapsed time versus SLO one-hour goal after detection; on miss record missed_slo true and continue
  [ACTION] if count would hit zero → emergency DEPLOY any allowed ready candidate and notify COORDINATOR immediately
  [RESULT] LINE_STATE repairing failover_ready health or needs_owner
  [FAIL] no allowed candidates → ESCALATE

::MODULE{ESCALATE|title:coordinator cover then owner}
  [TRIGGER] empty pool after expanded SCAN OR three platforms DEPLOY fail OR missing host capability OR node count zero after attempts
  [ACTION] COORDINATOR changes regions keywords platform types transport route or deploy route for EXECUTOR
  [ACTION] COORDINATOR retries once with the new strategy
  [ACTION] if still blocked: report OWNER with situation tried options remaining choices; wait decision
  [RESULT] resolved under COORDINATOR or OWNER_DECISION
  [FAIL] none; waiting is allowed

::MODULE{DELIVER|title:owner-facing output}
  [TRIGGER] at least one NODE_ACCEPTED on first run; update when replacements accept
  [ACTION] send QR secure file first; then short status: platforms exit cities dual or single plus backlog
  [ACTION] keep subscription versus URI distinction visible
  [ACTION] answer later OWNER questions like node status from REGISTRY without dumping secrets
  [RESULT] OWNER can scan and try; owner_device confirmed when they say so
  [NOTE] routine operations do not ping OWNER

::MODULE{ROTATE|title:proactive replacement before death}
  [TRIGGER] weekly evaluation or HEALTH finds trial expiry within three days or quota under about twenty percent or repeated soft enforcement signs
  [INPUT] REGISTRY expiry and quota fields
  [PREREQ] CANDIDATE_POOL has at least one ready different-platform candidate
  [ACTION] pre-DEPLOY replacement before the old node dies
  [ACTION] run ACCEPT on replacement; only then decommission old node
  [ACTION] goal is overlap without OWNER-visible downtime; if overlap impossible say degraded honestly
  [RESULT] rotation_log scrubbed; dual posture preserved when possible
  [FAIL] no candidate → ESCALATE while keeping old node alive

::MODULE{REGISTRY_IO|title:scrubbed bookkeeping}
  [TRIGGER] after every ACCEPT RECOVER SCAN decision
  [ACTION] update online nodes platforms exit_geo next_action_date scrubbed host class
  [ACTION] update accounts pointers into VAULT keys only
  [ACTION] update dead platforms with gate failure reason and cooldown
  [ACTION] update pool ready list
  [RESULT] single registry file under FILL_WORK_DIR readable by COORDINATOR for OWNER status answers
  [FAIL] never write live subscription bodies into registry markdown

::MODULE{HOW|title:end to end order}
  [STEP] 1 BOOT
  [STEP] 2 SCHED arm or mark on_call
  [STEP] 3 SCAN for a ready candidate and start delivery promptly; continue filling pool toward >=3 without blocking the first usable node
  [STEP] 4 loop DEPLOY and ACCEPT until two distinct platforms accepted or honest shortfall documented
  [STEP] 5 DELIVER to OWNER
  [STEP] 6 perpetual HEALTH with RECOVER ROTATE and SCAN under scheduler or on_call until OWNER stops

::MODULE{REPORT|title:machine readable status lines}
  [LINE] dual_online count and platform names scrubbed
  [LINE] pool_ready count
  [LINE] last_x_e2e timestamps per node scrubbed
  [LINE] SCHED_ARMED with fire evidence path or SCHED_ON_CALL
  [LINE] missed_slo flags if any
  [LINE] skipped_disallowed lanes this run
  [LINE] owner_device confirmed or pending
  [LINE] carrier_class muse|other|self

::RUBRIC{R1: dual ENGINEERING_BOOK markers|check:count|regex:"(?m)^::ILANG::v5\\.0::ENGINEERING_BOOK$"|expect:2}
::RUBRIC{R2: roles OWNER COORDINATOR EXECUTOR generic; Muse optional; method alias not account bind|check:human}
::RUBRIC{R3: dual-node and pool sizes stated as targets not completed facts|check:human}
::RUBRIC{R4: X public content required beyond generate_204|check:human}
::RUBRIC{R5: subscription versus node URI and secure QR specified|check:human}
::RUBRIC{R6: Waifly Free and Railway current personal-proxy bans skipped|check:human}
::RUBRIC{R7: terms gate is allowed-use not non-enforcement|check:human}
::RUBRIC{R8: scheduler authorized and fire-verified or honest on_call|check:human}
::RUBRIC{R9: one-hour recovery is goal not guarantee|check:human}
::RUBRIC{R10: no DIY command dump product for OWNER|check:human}
::RUBRIC{R11: runtime facts not hard-coded from attachment FACT|check:human}
::RUBRIC{R12: Chinese preface direct how-to from result to maintenance; blank-line paras not ideographic-space glue|check:human}
::RUBRIC{R13: modules expose trigger input prereq action result fail|check:human}
::RUBRIC{R14: each delivered node has real-client X content evidence, actual exit and disabled direct fallback|check:runtime}
::RUBRIC{R15: owner device is confirmed or explicitly pending; DNS and IPv6 routing checked|check:runtime}
::RUBRIC{R16: dual target shortfall and pool shortfall explicitly reported; no invented nodes|check:runtime}
::RUBRIC{R17: monitoring evidence is a real fire or pending, never dry-run described as live monitoring|check:runtime}

